WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:02.050
Hello.
你好。

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:03.490
Hi there.
嗨。

3
00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:04.030
Hi.
嗨。

4
00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.330
Welcome to our second drink of Halloween.
欢迎来到我们的第二期万圣节特饮节目。

5
00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:07.970
So guess what, Jenna?
猜猜怎么着，珍娜？

6
00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:13.010
According to pretty much every online poll, in fact, I didn't find one where this wasn't true.
根据几乎所有的在线民意调查，事实上，我没找到哪一个调查结果不是这样的。

7
00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:18.050
Season two Halloween is ranked as the number one office Halloween episode.
第二季的万圣节集被评为《办公室》里最棒的万圣节集。

8
00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:19.530
I don't doubt it.
我对此深信不疑。

9
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:20.590
I think it's my favorite.
我觉得这也是我最喜欢的一集。

10
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:26.150
I loved our breakdown of this episode because we had Creed in the studio for the entire episode.
我很喜欢我们对这一集的深度解析，因为克里德那一整集都在录音室里。

11
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.210
And he shared so many fun things.
他分享了好多有趣的事情。

12
00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.630
Well, Ange, I agree.
嗯，安吉，我同意。

13
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:35.670
And I actually panicked because I couldn't think of anything that we hadn't already shared about this episode.
其实我当时很慌，因为我想不出还有什么关于这一集是我们没分享过的。

14
00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:44.610
You guys, Angela and I have been dividing up, taking the lead on second drinks, and I was assigned to Halloween and I did not know what we were going to do.
各位，安吉拉和我一直在分工负责“第二杯特饮”节目，这次轮到我负责万圣节这一集，我当时真不知道我们还能聊些什么。

15
00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.210
I really felt like we shared it all.
我真的觉得我们已经把能说的都说了。

16
00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:48.950
But then, guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

17
00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:49.330
What?
怎么了？

18
00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:54.430
I found my old MySpace blog for this episode.
我找到了我当时为这一集写的 MySpace 博客。

19
00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:55.250
Old tech.
老古董技术了。

20
00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:55.850
Yes.
没错。

21
00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.310
And there were several tidbits that we never shared.
里面有好些我们从未分享过的趣闻。

22
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:00.610
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

23
00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:01.630
I'm so ready.
我准备好了。

24
00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:02.390
All right.
好极了。

25
00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:09.330
First off, Ange, in our breakdown, we talked about your cat costume and how your tail was very hard to sit in.
首先，安吉，在我们的解析里，我们聊到了你的猫咪装扮，还有那条尾巴让你坐着有多难受。

26
00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:16.110
But according to my blog, one of the ears on your costume kept falling down and it was ruining takes.
但根据我的博客，你服装上的一只耳朵总是往下掉，搞得我们一直在重拍。

27
00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:17.330
Do you remember this?
你还记得吗？

28
00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:25.870
I do remember this because sometimes I could feel it fall and be flat on my head and other times I couldn't.
我记得，因为有时候我能感觉到它掉下来贴在头顶上，但有时候又感觉不到。

29
00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:30.150
And so I would start talking and Oscar would be like, your ear is gone.
所以我刚开始说话，奥斯卡就会说，你的耳朵又掉了。

30
00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:35.010
But I completely forgot about that until you reminded me.
直到你提醒我，我才完全想起来。

31
00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.830
And I was like, oh, yes, it was driving us crazy.
当时我就想，噢，没错，那可真是把我们折磨疯了。

32
00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:46.570
Well, I also shared that you broke several cookies in that scene that we had together in the conference room.
我还分享过你在会议室那场戏里弄碎了好几块饼干。

33
00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:54.470
You know, the one where you ask me what I brought and I say brownies and you're like really pissed off because you're like same category as you brought cookies.
你知道的，就是你问我带了什么，我说布朗尼，然后你特别生气，因为你觉得那和饼干属于同一类。

34
00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:56.790
And then I like slam the tray down.
然后我就把托盘重重地摔在桌上。

35
00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:57.290
Yes.
没错。

36
00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:04.310
In my blog, I wrote this, quote, Angela kept slamming them down on the plate in disgust during the scene.
我在博客里是这么写的，引用一下：“安吉拉在拍那场戏时，一直厌恶地把饼干摔在盘子上。”

37
00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.070
I actually remember us breaking.
我其实记得我们当时笑场了。

38
00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:09.730
I remember laughing because I broke them.
我记得我笑是因为我把饼干弄碎了。

39
00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:13.510
And it's got to live somewhere in some blooper land.
那段花絮肯定还在某个地方存着。

40
00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:22.590
It muSt. I mean, we talked about how that was a hard scene to get through, but I failed to mention that you were destroying cookies with one ear.
肯定在。我是说，我们聊过那场戏有多难拍，但我忘了提你当时是一只耳朵耷拉着在毁坏饼干。

41
00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:22.961
Sure.
确实。

42
00:02:22.961 --> 00:02:28.370
Now, this episode also features the very first Jim and Pam air high five.
另外，这一集还有吉姆和帕姆的第一次空中击掌。

43
00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:28.850
Mm hmm.
嗯哼。

44
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.010
I know we talked about it because I love it.
我知道我们聊过这个，因为我太喜欢那一幕了。

45
00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:36.550
Yes, we discussed it, but we did not talk about how that was an improvisation.
是的，我们讨论过，但我们没提过那是即兴发挥。

46
00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:39.190
That was not scripted, lady.
那不是剧本里写的，女士。

47
00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.290
So wait, it wasn't in the shooting draft?
等等，所以拍摄剧本里没有这一段？

48
00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:44.310
No, I can't believe I didn't share this the first time.
没有，真不敢相信我第一次竟然没分享这个。

49
00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:52.690
In fact, there wasn't any description in the script for how Pam reacts to Jim pretending to be Michael Scott on the phone.
事实上，剧本里根本没有描述帕姆在吉姆假装成迈克尔·斯科特打电话时该有什么反应。

50
00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:57.330
He does this impression of Michael because they're tricking Dwight.
他模仿迈克尔是因为他们正在捉弄德怀特。

51
00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:57.590
Yeah.
没错。

52
00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:00.390
And when he hangs up, we do the air high five.
等他挂断电话，我们就击个空气掌。

53
00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.210
But in the script, it says nothing.
但剧本里什么都没写。

54
00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.250
It doesn't even say Pam looks delighted.
甚至没写帕姆看起来很高兴。

55
00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:11.190
And my memory is that John suggested that we air high five to give it a little button at the end.
我记得是约翰提议我们击个空气掌，给结尾加点小点缀。

56
00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:15.090
We nailed it the first time and everyone freaked out on how cute it was.
我们一次就成功了，大家都觉得这太可爱了，激动不已。

57
00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:15.990
It was super cute.
真的超级可爱。

58
00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:19.610
It's also the no look, the no look air high five.
而且还是那种不看对方的，不看对方的空气击掌。

59
00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:20.350
It's special.
很特别。

60
00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:22.850
It's like, oh, these two are in sync.
就像是，噢，这两个人真有默契。

61
00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.030
What's going to happen with these characters?
这两个角色接下来会发生什么呢？

62
00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:26.830
Well, this is where it all began.
嗯，这就是一切开始的地方。

63
00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:28.210
I love it.
我喜欢。

64
00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:39.410
And then, Angela, according to my MySpace blog about this episode, Paul Lieberstein improvised a line in his scene with Steve that made Steve break.
然后，安吉拉，根据我当时写这集剧评的MySpace博客，保罗·利伯斯坦在他和史蒂夫的对手戏里即兴加了一句台词，让史蒂夫笑场了。

65
00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:43.830
And I wrote that it took Steve two full minutes to recover.
我当时写道，史蒂夫足足花了整整两分钟才恢复过来。

66
00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:47.590
And I'm like, wow, how did we not talk about this?
我心想，哇，我们怎么没聊过这个？

67
00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:50.770
I checked our breakdown and sure enough, we had not discussed it.
我查了我们的剧集分析，果然，我们没讨论过。

68
00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:51.770
I went back.
我回去看了一下。

69
00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:52.830
I watched the episode.
我看了那一集。

70
00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:55.590
There are not any scenes between Toby and Michael.
托比和迈克尔之间根本没有对手戏。

71
00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.870
It's a deleted scene.
那是删减片段。

72
00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:04.490
Oh, I must have written this MySpace blog before I knew what the episode was actually going to be when it aired.
噢，我一定是在这集播出前，还没确定最终成片内容时写的那个MySpace博客。

73
00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:05.070
Right, right.
对，没错。

74
00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:13.070
So there's this deleted scene where Toby asks Michael for the name of the employee that is going to be fired so that he can start the HR paperwork.
所以有个删减片段，托比问迈克尔要被解雇员工的名字，好让他开始准备人事文件。

75
00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:16.330
And Michael tries to fire Toby.
然后迈克尔试图解雇托比。

76
00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:20.570
I found it and I thought we should listen to it.
我找到了那个片段，觉得我们应该听听。

77
00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:21.210
OK.
好。

78
00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:22.210
Michael.
迈克尔。

79
00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:27.310
Michael, do you have the name of the employee?
迈克尔，你有那个员工的名字了吗？

80
00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:28.570
The employee you're letting go?
你要解雇的那个员工？

81
00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:30.170
I'd like to start working on our placement.
我想开始着手处理安置事宜了。

82
00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:32.170
Fine.
行啊。

83
00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:36.870
If you are so anxious to see a head roll, it's you.
如果你这么急着看人头落地，那个人就是你。

84
00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:38.450
There.
给你。

85
00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:40.210
You brought it on yourself.
是你自找的。

86
00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:41.230
Too bad.
太可惜了。

87
00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:43.610
Can't say that I'm sorry.
我可没法说我很抱歉。

88
00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:44.550
It's a relief.
这简直是一种解脱。

89
00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:46.650
I don't report to you, Michael.
我不向你汇报，迈克尔。

90
00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:48.350
I report to the head of HR in New York.
我向纽约的人事部主管汇报。

91
00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.250
You asked for a name.
你问我要名字。

92
00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:50.090
I gave you a name.
我给你名字了。

93
00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.530
Now you're not doing your job.
现在是你没在履行职责。

94
00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:52.430
Why don't you just resign?
你为什么不干脆辞职呢？

95
00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.690
If you just sent someone else, you need to have an HR representative.
如果你只是派别人去，你也需要有人事代表在场。

96
00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:01.130
Just know that if I could have fired you, I would have.
你要知道，如果我能解雇你，我早就解雇你了。

97
00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:03.770
I know, Michael.
我知道，迈克尔。

98
00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:06.510
What line made him laugh?
哪句台词让他笑场了？

99
00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:07.810
Well, that's the thing.
嗯，问题就在这儿。

100
00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:11.790
I said that it was some improvisation that made Steve lose it.
我当时说是因为某种即兴发挥才让史蒂夫破功的。

101
00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:16.810
I was clearly sitting in the background at reception observing this whole thing be shot.
我当时显然坐在接待处背景里，看着这一切被拍摄下来。

102
00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:20.450
But I checked the script and it's exactly as scripted.
但我查了剧本，内容和剧本里写的一模一样。

103
00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:23.450
So I guess maybe the improv didn't make it in the cut.
所以我猜即兴发挥的部分可能没被剪进正片里。

104
00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:28.130
But I do know that if anyone could make Steve break, it was Paul.
但我确实知道，如果有人能让史蒂夫笑场，那一定是保罗。

105
00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:31.550
I feel like it's the moment just very resigned.
我觉得那一刻他表现得非常无奈。

106
00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:33.070
He says, I know, Michael.
他说，我知道，迈克尔。

107
00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.730
That's my guess.
我是这么猜的。

108
00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:44.770
Well, finally, Angela, I shared in my MySpace blog that Rain, John, and Brian held their first
好吧，最后，安吉拉，我在我的MySpace博客上分享过，雷恩、约翰和布莱恩在拍摄这一集期间，

109
00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:50.890
ever PlayStation 2 boxing contest during our downtime for this episode.
举办了他们有史以来第一次PlayStation 2拳击比赛。

110
00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:54.810
But I guess the episode finished shooting before they could finish the tournament.
但我猜在他们打完比赛之前，这一集就已经拍完了。

111
00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:59.470
I noted that Rain and John were down to their final fighters.
我记得当时雷恩和约翰都只剩下最后一名选手了。

112
00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:01.890
That just brings me right back.
这一下子把我带回了过去。

113
00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:02.430
I know.
我知道。

114
00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:06.210
Those guys, we'd be in a scene and they'd be like, okay, last take, last take.
那些家伙，我们拍戏的时候，他们总会说，好了，最后一条，最后一条。

115
00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:07.010
We got to go.
我们得走了。

116
00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:10.850
We're like, guys, are you doing your boxing match or are we doing the scene?
我们就会说，伙计们，你们是在打拳击比赛，还是我们要拍戏啊？

117
00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:11.950
Pretty much.
差不多就是这样。

118
00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.370
Well, that's a really fun second drink, lady.
好吧，这第二杯饮料真不错，女士。

119
00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:14.990
Thank you.
谢谢。

120
00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:16.370
I was very excited.
我当时非常兴奋。

121
00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:20.330
Well, everyone, we hope you like this breakdown of Halloween.
好了，各位，希望你们喜欢我们对《万圣节》这一集的解析。

122
00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:23.510
Like Angela said, it's with our dear friend Creed Bratton.
就像安吉拉说的，这次我们请到了亲爱的朋友克里德·布拉顿。

123
00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:24.890
It's a really good one.
这一集真的很棒。

124
00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:26.270
Creed is so fun.
克里德太有趣了。

125
00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:27.290
You're going to love it.
你们一定会喜欢的。

126
00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:27.930
All right.
好的。

127
00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:28.630
Here it is.
开始了。

128
00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:29.090
Enjoy.
尽情享受吧。

129
00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:34.270
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

130
00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:35.590
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

131
00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:36.870
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

132
00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:38.090
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

133
00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:41.930
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们正为你们制作终极《办公室》重温播客。

134
00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:46.310
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes
每周，我们都会解析一集《办公室》，并分享独家幕后故事，

135
00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:48.910
stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
这些故事只有我们两个亲历者才能告诉你们。

136
00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:50.070
We're The Office, ladies.
我们是《办公室》的女士们。

137
00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:52.860
I love it.
我喜欢这个。

138
00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:54.300
Creed is here.
克里德来了。

139
00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:55.100
Creed is here.
克里德来了。

140
00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:56.020
Creed is here.
克里德来了。

141
00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:57.480
Creed is in the house.
克里德到场了。

142
00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:57.840
Yeah.
耶。

143
00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:00.860
This is so amazing.
这太棒了。

144
00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:03.520
Creed's going to be with us for the whole episode, guys.
伙计们，克里德会全程陪着我们。

145
00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:08.100
Okay, Creed, you are our first in-house visitor, right?
好的，克里德，你是我们第一位到访录音室的嘉宾，对吧？

146
00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:11.060
I mean, we've had people call in, but you're our first in-house gueSt.
我是说，我们之前有连线过嘉宾，但你是第一位亲临现场的。

147
00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:12.220
I'm the first one.
我是第一个。

148
00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:14.640
I might have a bathroom break or something.
我可能得去上个厕所什么的。

149
00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:16.440
